  H.264 with B-frames has decode order ≠ presentation order. The ctts box or composition_time_offset in trun handles this. If:                           
  - FFmpeg restart produces different CTO patterns                                                                                                       
  - Our segmenter doesn't preserve these correctly                                                                                                       
  - Values become negative or overflow in ways FFmpeg 6 doesn't handle                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                         
  ...the decoder might get confused about when to display frames.                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                         
